// Velox V2 — Strategy Lab. PACT Finance. RESEARCH CODE: it makes no claim of profitability and is not financial advice.
//
// Velox V1's supply & demand engine (zones, order blocks, breakers, FVGs, BOS/CHoCH, higher-timeframe zones), run as a
// STRATEGY so TradingView's broker emulator fills the orders. One entry, one structural stop, one target in R.
//
// Execution model (deliberate):
//  - The setup is decided when a candle CLOSES. The market order fills at the NEXT candle's open
//    (process_orders_on_close = false), so nothing is filled inside the candle that created the signal.
//  - Stop = the level's far edge + an ATR buffer. If that stop is too small or too big, the trade is SKIPPED, never widened.
//  - The target is re-anchored to the actual fill price, so every trade really is targetRR × its own risk.
//  - Size = risk cash ÷ stop distance, so every trade risks about the same (default $100 = 1R). Net profit ÷ 100 ≈ net R.
//  - Bar Magnifier is OFF in code (requesting it on a non-Premium plan stops the strategy). On Premium, tick it in
//    Properties: a candle that touches both stop and target is then resolved on lower-timeframe data.
//  - Costs: commission 0.15 per ounce per side (≈ 3 pips round trip) as a placeholder. Set YOUR broker's in Properties.
//  - Flat before the weekend (Friday 15:00 New York) by default, so no fill is assumed across the weekend gap.
//
// Research table: every closed trade is stored with its setup (side, zone/OB, session, strength, FVG, HTF zone, age)
// and its result in R measured from the real fill and real profit after costs, plus MFE / MAE in R.
// MFE / MAE are approximate on the exit candle (the order of prices inside one candle is unknown).

//@version=6
strategy("Velox V2 — Strategy Lab", "Velox V2 Lab", overlay = true, pyramiding = 0, calc_on_every_tick = false, calc_on_order_fills = false, process_orders_on_close = false, use_bar_magnifier = false, initial_capital = 10000, currency = currency.USD, default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1, commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract, commission_value = 0.15, slippage = 0, margin_long = 5, margin_short = 5, max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_bars_back = 500)

// Heikin Ashi, Renko and other synthetic candles produce fills that never existed.
if barstate.isfirst and not chart.is_standard
    runtime.error("Velox V2 Strategy Lab must run on standard candles (not Heikin Ashi, Renko, Range, etc.).")

// ═════════════════════════════ Inputs ═════════════════════════════

